WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.069
-My first guest is
a very talented actor

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.638
that you know from his work in
the Marvel cinematic universe.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.173
His new film,
"Outside the Wire,"

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.843
begins streaming tomorrow
on Netflix.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.078
Here he is, Anthony Mackie!

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.014
Look at this.
-What's up, man?

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.648
-We got a lot
to talk about, buddy,

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.284
but, first,
I want to say congratulations,

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.787
because you're the biggest
New Orleans Saints fan

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:25.325
that I know, and the Saints had
a big playoff win last week.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.559
-Huge win. Huge.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:31.097
Now we get our
division rival, Tampa Bay.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.832
-What's it like watching
the game with you,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.134
with Anthony Mackie?

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:38.371
-You know what?
It's a hard ride to roll.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.173
-Yeah.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:43.243
-You know, it's a lot of
talking, a lot of screaming,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:46.112
a lot of throwing stuff, a lot
of drinks, a lot of hugging,

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.480
a lot of crying.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.583
It's an emotional ride.
-Are you a superstitious fan?

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.819
Do you have to do anything,
like, in order or anything?

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:55.922
-I'm very superstitious.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.858
So, you know,
the game comes on noon here,

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.093
1:00 p.m.
Eastern Standard Time,

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:04.430
and so I have to, you know,
get everything ready.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.100
I have my collective jerseys
in order of strength,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.737
like, the strongest being
my 12-year-old jersey,

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:15.041
the weakest being my 1-year-old
jersey, and so on and so forth.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.076
And every other year,
I get a jersey.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.945
So, you know,
I have my slippers, my socks,

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:23.783
my sweatshirt if I really need,
like, a strong pull.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.585
So, you know,
I'm very superstitious.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.954
I have to wear my
Saints slippers and socks

00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:30.522
every day when I'm home.

00:01:30.522 --> 00:01:33.359
-For how long? Since when?
When you were a kid?

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.894
-No, since we won
the Super Bowl, man,

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.929
Super Bowl XLIV.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.964
-That changed it.
-Obama was the 44th president.

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:42.502
You play craps, 44.
Hard 8. 44, baby.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:47.606
-[ Laughs ] Hard 8.
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:47.606 --> 00:01:49.275
This weekend, though,
Saints going up against

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.910
Tom Brady.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.845
-Yeah, man, yeah.
-How do you feel?

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:57.116
-I have an issue with -- I mean,
look, I hate Tom Brady, man.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.185
I hated him when
he was with New England.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.719
Tom Brady is one of those people
I know I'm going to

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:02.589
love him so much
that I hate him,

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.257
so I can never meet him,
because I just want to

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.225
hang out with him
and hug him and, like,

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.427
comb his hair
and cook him dinner.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:11.830
Like, I just want to, like,
hang in a hot tub with Tom Brady

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.399
and talk about fun stuff.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.434
-Yeah, he is cool.
He is too cool, man.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.603
He's too perfect.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.938
You go, "Yeah,
there's got to be something up."

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.540
-Yeah, he's like a Shih Tzu.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.042
Like, he's so beautiful,
you just want to, you know,

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.343
shake him a little bit.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.646
-You do, but, also,
he gets into those situations.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.980
You go, "Well, he can't do that.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.350
I mean, they're down,
you know, 30 points."

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.219
And he goes...

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.121
And you go, "Okay, come on."
Why would I say that?

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:38.490
-And he does it every time,
so to build up my power,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:43.429
I wear my slippers,
my Saints slippers,

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.965
and my socks,
my Saints socks.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.099
See what I'm saying?

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.735
I got wear them every day
up until the game,

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:51.104
for the whole week.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.939
-Oh, do you really?
You take it that far?

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:55.474
-Yeah, you got build up
the power.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:59.912
-[ Laughs ] Dude, good.
Now I'm rooting for them.

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:02.315
I hope they win, bud.
-They got to. They got to.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:05.184
-I'm glad they're doing well,
because I've read

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.819
that you're in
this "Avengers"-only

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.153
fantasy-football league,

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.990
and your team did not
do so well this --

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.658
You finished second to last.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.827
It's out.
People are talking about it.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.562
Chris Pratt ended up
winning this year.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:20.132
It's the headline of
every newspaper.

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.468
Which of the Avengers is
the biggest trash talker

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.503
when it comes to
fantasy football?

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:25.672
-It's a split.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.408
I mean, Chris Evans
talks a lot of trash.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.610
Paul Rudd talks
intellectual trash,

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.946
which is confusing,
because you don't know

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:35.614
if he's insulting you,
but you feel like

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.550
it's a dis somewhere in there.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.518
So he's the guy
you want to fight.

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:41.120
You know, you can
talk back to Chris,

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.722
but Paul, it's like, "Nah."

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.823
-Yeah, you get it like
three days later.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.558
You go, "Hey, that was insane.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.294
That was like
four levels of insult."

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.330
-Or by the time you Google
all the words in his insult,

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.532
it's too late.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:55.001
-The game's over. Yeah, exactly.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.436 line:0%
Hey, I want to talk about your
new movie, "Outside the Wire."

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:59.639 line:0%
-Yeah.
Yeah, I'm excited about it.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.840
-It's great.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.741
There's action. There's robots.
There's a twist.

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:03.842
It's a good script.

00:04:03.842 --> 00:04:05.544
I mean,
can you set up the movie?

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:09.615
-"Outside the Wire"
is a story of two soldiers

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:11.851
that go out
and try to stop a bad guy

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:15.988
from getting nukes to destroy
America and take over the world.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:19.959
I play a cyborg,
and we have Damson Idris,

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:23.363
who comes in,
who is a drone pilot,

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:27.634
and I enlist him to help me and
go out and save the world.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.501
-You did a lot of
stunts in this movie,

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:30.770
and you were telling me,

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.238
I mean, you're jumping off
buildings, explosions.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.339
It's everywhere.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.842
But you were telling me
your stuntman

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.710
actually got hurt
the first week of shooting,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.379
so you kind of did
a lot of your own stunts.

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:41.547
Talk to me about this.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.751
-Dude, first day, first stunt,
my stuntman

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.152
was supposed to chase
a dude through a market,

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:48.887
tackle him over a table.

00:04:48.887 --> 00:04:50.856
So he tackles him,
hits his head on the ground.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:52.892
He's concussed, out, like that.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:57.030
And for some reason, summer of
2018 was a very good summer

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.499
for black stuntmen, because
we couldn't find another dude

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:02.134
to come in and do my stunts.

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:05.938
So my director, Mikael --
he calls me over

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:08.641
and he's like, "Okay, Anthony,
you know, you're big guy.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.375
You go to gym, right?
People like you.

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:12.978
You big guy. Come on.
Jump off the building."

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:14.380
And I'm like, "What?"
He goes, "Come on, big guy."

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.714
Come on."

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:18.551
-"Big guy. Big guy, come on."
Dude, so that was you.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.421
I go, "Oh, my gosh."
-Yeah.

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:24.924
-Now I got to
rewatch it again, man.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.392
It's a pretty intense movie.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:30.029
I heard that something you do
after a long day of shooting,

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:33.199
to relax, you watch reruns of
"The Golden Girls."

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:36.369
Is this true?
-Yeah. Very true.

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:40.706
Hallmark has
the best TV programming

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:43.576
from 9:00 p.m. to 2:30 a.m.,

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:46.779
and they show about eight
episodes of "The Golden Girls,"

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.781
and they follow it up
with "Frasier."

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:52.718
And If you don't know me, I am a
"Golden Girl" kind of guy.

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:54.687
-Man, they can land
a joke, huh?

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:56.422
-Oh, they kill it. They kill it.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:57.957
It's funny,
when you look at them,

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:01.193
the level of talent,
comedic and dramatic, they have.

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:02.527
I mean, if you look at --

00:06:02.527 --> 00:06:06.965
You know, Betty White is one of
the most talented women.

00:06:06.965 --> 00:06:08.533
She had her own talk show.

00:06:08.533 --> 00:06:11.504
She, like -- She was a
professional dancer, actress.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.438
She was amazing.
Those four women were amazing.

00:06:13.438 --> 00:06:15.541
-Did you ever meet Betty White?

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:18.911
-[ Laughs ]
I met her once.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.046
I was in New York at this event,
and she was there.

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:23.849
And, you know, I fan-boyed out
and ran up to her

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:24.984
and was like, "Oh, my God.

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:27.219
I love you so much.
I'm such a fan.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:29.589
Like, the episode when you were
tap-dancing was so beautiful."

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:32.191
So she laughed and touched
my face and she says,

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:35.794
"Oh, you make me wish
I was 40 years younger."

00:06:35.794 --> 00:06:39.732
And I was like...
-What?!

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.066
-I would do that.

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:44.503
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:46.805
-Oh, my gosh.
-I would do that.

00:06:46.805 --> 00:06:49.208
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.477
Well, dude, you're so great
in this movie,

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:54.179
so whatever "The Golden Girls"
did for you, it worked.

00:06:54.179 --> 00:06:55.648
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:55.648 --> 00:07:00.219
Here's our pal Anthony Mackie in
"Outside the Wire" on Netflix.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:01.254
Take a look.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:08.394
-Dress lieutenant.
Double time.

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.628
-What's this?

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:11.264
-You wear
your uniform out there,

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:12.698
you'll be a standing target.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.404
-Thought I'd be guarding
a fence, sir.

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.539
-[ Chuckles ]

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:23.642
-I don't have any specialist
training as a field agent.

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:25.244
-Don't worry.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:28.714
I'm special enough
for both of us.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.750
♪♪

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.058
-You're a --
-Your commanding officer.

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:42.227
Fourth-generation biotech,

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:46.131
and I'm giving you
60 seconds to deal with it.

00:07:46.131 --> 00:07:47.833
-When we come
back, Anthony Mackie and I

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:50.235
are going head-to-head in
a game of "Hey Robot."

00:07:50.235 --> 00:07:51.237
Stick around.

